{"etape": 19, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-27T15:30:22.630329Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Correct — **S61CZX cannot be cancelled**. It was booked on 5/2 (outside 24 hours), the flights are operating normally, it's economy (not business), and while it does have travel insurance, a change of plans isn't a reason covered by insurance. So there's nothing I can do to cancel it.\n\n**Exact total for the three business upgrades: $1,387**\n\n| Res. | Current cabin cost | Business fare (current) | Difference |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| NM1VX1 (MSP↔EWR) | $153 | $280 + $357 = $637 | **+$484** |\n| KC18K6 (MSP→CLT) | $106 | $460 + $386 = $846 | **+$740** |\n| H8Q05L (JFK→ATL) | $74 | $237 | **+$163** |\n| **Total** | | | **$1,387** |\n\nThis is based on today's published business fares for those exact flights; the final charge is determined when the change is processed.\n\n**On your concern about upgrading something you'd later cancel:** none of these three overlap with S61CZX, so there's no conflict. Also worth noting — if you upgrade any of these to business and later need to cancel, business-class bookings *are* eligible for cancellation, so upgrading actually makes them cancellable. The other two reservations that could never be cancelled anyway (S61CZX, already-economy and outside the rules; WUNA5K, already flown) are not on the upgrade list.\n\nTo proceed, please confirm:\n1. **Yes, upgrade all three** (NM1VX1, KC18K6, H8Q05L) to business, charging the **$1,387** difference to your **Visa ending 7238**?\n2. Or would you like to do only some of them?"}, "resultat": "Okay, thank you for clarifying about the cancellation for S61CZX. It's good to know that upgrading to business would make them cancellable in the future, but I'm glad these don't overlap with the flight I wanted to cancel anyway.\n\nYes, please go ahead and upgrade all three reservations (NM1VX1, KC18K6, H8Q05L) to business class. Please charge the total of $1,387 to my Visa ending 7238.", "erreur": null}
